<h2>Wednesday, June 16,  2004</h2>	
<div class="post">
	 <h3 class="storytitle" id="post-24"><a href="http://www.marksportal.net/index.php?p=24" rel="bookmark" title="Permanent Link: Today is Wednesday!">Today is Wednesday!</a></h3>
	<div class="meta">posted by: Mark @ 10:00 pm </div>
	
	<div id="wplinks" class="storycontent">
			<p>Today is Wednesday and there is really nothing to say, so I will ramble as long as I can&#8230;.Work has been so busy that I haven&#8217;t really had a chance to spend time with God during my lunch hour.  It&#8217;s been a bit disappointing as I&#8217;m eager to spend time with Him.  I tried to spend a bit of time with God today, but due to allergies and such, I was distracted easily.  Quite a bummer.   I spent a brief time in Hebrews reading about the Order of Melchizedek and how Abraham tithed 10% of all he owned to Melchizedek.   </p>
	<p>Well, it&#8217;s late and since I really don&#8217;t have much to say, I won&#8217;t go on.
</p>
	</div>
	
